const research=[
{n:'B · 01',layerzh:'方法层',layeren:'Methods',zh:'建成环境视觉智能',en:'Built Environment Visual Intelligence',img:'/research/visual-intelligence.png',zhd:'本研究提出一种利用街景全景图像估算高层商务区玻璃幕墙反射日光时空分布的方法。通过太阳路径映射、全景投影变换与矩阵计算，量化反射发生的位置、持续时间和强度，并揭示季节、城市形态与立面朝向的影响，为城市反射风险识别、规划评估和环境治理提供可视化工具。',end:'This study develops a street-view panorama–based method for estimating where and when sunlight reflected by glass curtain walls affects surrounding streets. It combines solar-path mapping, panoramic projection transformation, and matrix-based calculations to quantify the location, duration, and intensity of reflected sunlight, supporting visual risk detection, environmental assessment, and map-based communication.',paper:'A method of estimating the spatiotemporal distribution of reflected sunlight from glass curtain walls in high-rise business districts using street-view panoramas',meta:'Sustainable Cities and Society · 79 · 103671 · 2022',authors:'Haipeng Zhu, Zongchao Gu',doi:'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scs.2022.103671',altzh:'九幅场地平面图展示玻璃幕墙反射辐照强度和热点的逐时变化。',alten:'Nine site maps show hourly changes in reflected irradiance and hotspot locations.'},
{n:'A · 02',layerzh:'机制层',layeren:'Mechanisms',zh:'环境视觉与空间认知',en:'Environmental Vision & Spatial Cognition',img:'/research/environmental-vision.png',zhd:'本研究以苏州留园绿荫轩为例，在沉浸式虚拟现实环境中结合深度判断实验与眼动追踪，考察观景位置、景框形态和外围环境信息如何影响视觉深度感知。结果表明，景框外围的环境背景能够显著增强空间深度体验，为理解传统园林的空间认知机制和循证设计提供实验依据。',end:'Using the Lvyin Pavilion in the Lingering Garden as a case, this study examines how viewing position, frame geometry, and peripheral environmental information shape visual depth perception. A controlled immersive virtual-reality experiment combines depth-estimation tasks with eye tracking, providing experimental evidence for spatial cognition and evidence-based design in classical Chinese gardens.',paper:'Effects of scenery frame on visual depth perception in classical Chinese gardens: A case study of the Lvyin Pavilion in Lingering Garden',meta:'Frontiers of Architectural Research · 14(2) · 402–415 · 2025',authors:'Haipeng Zhu, Yuhang Kong, Hong Zhang, Zongchao Gu, Ryuzo Ohno',doi:'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foar.2024.08.009',altzh:'六幅热图比较三类场景在两次测试中的视觉注意分布。',alten:'Six heat maps compare visual-attention distributions for three scene conditions across two tests.'},
{n:'C · 03',layerzh:'应用与转译层',layeren:'Application & translation',zh:'数字遗产与设计转译',en:'Digital Heritage & Design Translation',img:'/research/digital-heritage.png',zhd:'人们在建成环境中的运动视觉体验，由于环境界面间的相互遮蔽，常伴随遮蔽处新信息的出现以及旧信息的消失。该视觉信息的更新过程常引发观察者的视觉注意以及对环境继续探索的兴趣。在新数据环境下，全景视觉技术为全视域、定量化研究动态视觉信息变量提供了新思路。本文基于视觉生态学理论，通过全景光流视角解析“偏倚视景”现象中的视觉更新机制，并借助全景投影变换及其图像特征，分别提出基于实地摄影与模型渲染数据的视觉信息更新量测度和分析方法。本文选取苏州古典园林曲廊空间、室外展廊空间为研究对象，应用所提出的方法定量化、可视化分析游观过程中的视觉信息更新规律与特征，探讨视觉信息更新量对人们视觉引导的作用。本研究突破固定视角、局部视野、静态视觉信息分析框架，创新性地提出运动视角、全视域、动态视觉信息分析方法，并通过实证研究验证方法可行性。未来研究可结合认知实验探讨“偏倚视景”中视觉更新变量与主观感知之间的作用机制。',end:'People\'s visual experience of motion in built environments is often accompanied by the appearance of new information and the disappearance of old information at the occluding edge due to the mutual masking of environmental interfaces. The process of updating this visual information often triggers the observer\'s visual attention and interest in continuing to explore the environment. In the new data environment, panoramic vision technology provides a new way of thinking for the study of dynamic visual information variables in the full field of view quantitatively. Based on the theoretical foundation of visual ecology, this paper reanalyses the mechanism of visual renewal through the perspective of panoramic optical flow and proposes a method for measuring and analysing the amount of visual information renewal based on field photography and model rendering data with the help of panoramic projection transformation and its image characteristics, respectively. The study selects the curved corridor space and outdoor exhibition space of a Suzhou classical garden as the research objects and apply the proposed method to quantify and visually analyse the rules and characteristics of visual information updating in the process of touring, so as to explore the role of the amount of visual information updating in guiding people\'s vision. This study breaks through the framework of fixed perspective, local field of view, and static visual information analysis, and innovatively proposes the method of motion perspective, full field of view, and dynamic visual information analysis, and verifies the feasibility of the method through empirical research. Future studies can combine cognitive experiments to explore the mechanism of the role of visual updating variables in subjective perception.',paper:'“偏倚视景”空间机制解析：基于全景图像的环境视觉更新测度方法初探',paperEn:'Analysis of the Spatial Mechanism of the "Veduta per Angolo": A Preliminary Study on Measurement Methods for Ambient Visual Information Deletion and Accretion at the Occluding Edge Based on Panoramic Images',meta:'《世界建筑》 · 2026(5) · 96–102',metaEn:'World Architecture · 2026(5) · 96–102',authors:'朱海鹏、孔宇航、顾宗超',authorsEn:'Haipeng Zhu, Yuhang Kong, Zongchao Gu',doi:'https://doi.org/10.16414/j.wa.20260407.001',altzh:'两组分析图比较空间围合界面和天空界面的视觉更新，并与平面和剖面对齐。',alten:'Two analytical groups compare visual updates in the spatial-enclosure and sky interfaces, aligned with plan and section.'}
];
research[0].abstractEn='Obtaining the time and location of sunlight reflection within a street environment is important to improve the comfort and safety of public spaces. This paper proposes a method to estimate the spatiotemporal distribution of sunlight reflection within a street based on street-view data. First, the solar path on the panorama is plotted to obtain the potential orientation of the radiation source and the reflection on building facades. Next, the continuous time–date distribution of direct and reflected sunlight at a certain site is obtained by the panoramic projection transformation approach. The accumulative duration and time-series parameters of the reflected scenario are estimated by a matrix operation. By mapping the time-specific duration of the sunlight reflection scene, we can obtain the spatiotemporal distribution within the street network. We applied the proposed method to a case study in a high-rise business district and quantified the range, duration, and intensity of reflected sunlight in the surrounding area. Seasonal changes, city morphology, and facade orientation were found to be the factors affecting the distribution tendency of reflected sunlight. The risk detection, visualization, and quantification analysis results on sunlight reflection can provide a reference for city management, urban planning, and environmental evaluation.';
research[1].abstractEn='Visual depth (distance) perception is a fundamental aspect of environmental cognition, as it allows people to judge the spatial scale of their surroundings. However, estimating the depth of classical Chinese gardens is challenging, especially from static viewpoints that frame the scenery. Previous studies have examined how the internal components of the scenery frame affect depth perception. Still, the role of the frame and its peripheral information as environmental background have been largely overlooked. This study investigates how depth perception at viewpoints is influenced by viewing position displacement, frame geometry, and environmental context. The authors created nine stimulus materials in a cave virtual reality environment (three image treatments × three positions). Seventy-one participants were asked to evaluate depth perception using the magnitude estimation and adjustment methods. Their eye movement behavior was also recorded using an eye-movement instrument (SensoMotoric Instruments (SMI) eye-tracking glasses, 120 Hz). The results showed that participants could perceive spatial depth differences between viewing positions even when the internal viewpoint displacement was small; frame shape did not significantly affect depth perception and gaze behavior; and peripheral visual information of the frame enhanced depth perception significantly. Moreover, the form of the environmental background, especially the position of the scenery window, strongly guided the participants’ gaze. These findings suggest that ambient visual information significantly impacts environmental experience, which landscape designers should consider.';
